From: Yocto Wrynose migration
Subject: [PATCH] essos: use time64-compatible input event fields

On 32-bit targets using 64-bit time_t, linux/input.h exposes input event
timestamps through input_event_sec and input_event_usec instead of time.

Upstream-Status: Pending

---
 essos.cpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/essos.cpp b/essos.cpp
--- a/essos.cpp
+++ b/essos.cpp
@@ -3952,7 +3952,7 @@ void essProcessInputDevices(EssCtx* ctx)
                            default:
                               {
                                  int keyCode= e.code;
-                                 long long timeMillis= e.time.tv_sec*1000LL+e.time.tv_usec/1000LL;
+                                 long long timeMillis= e.input_event_sec*1000LL+e.input_event_usec/1000LL;
 
                                  switch ( e.value )
                                  {
